Pursae — third-party notices
==================================

Pursae is licensed under the GNU General Public License, version 2 or (at your option) any later
version (LICENSE). It bundles the third-party components listed below; each keeps its own license.
The full texts of those licenses are in LICENSES/ (see LICENSES/README.md); the permissive licenses
(MIT, BSD, ISC, …) are reproduced there once as a template, and the copyright holders they refer to
are named in this file. Where a component ships its own license file in the tree, that file is named.

Versions come from the files' own headers, WordPress' script registry
(internal/server/defaults/wp-registry.json, "ver"), package-lock.json or go.sum.

Pursae's earlier page builder, derived from Elementor, was removed in 0.4.1 (migrations 0005–0007
are empty steps).

Contents
  1. WordPress core files (web/wp-includes, web/wp-admin)
  2. Libraries bundled by WordPress core
  3. WordPress block editor (Gutenberg) packages
  4. Themes and fonts
  5. Pursae Web Builder (web/web-builder, builder/)
  6. Pursae Flipbook (web/flipbook/vendor)
  7. Maps, geolocation data and translations
  8. Go modules compiled into the wpgo binary
  9. Docker image


