7. Maps, geolocation data and translations
------------------------------------------
* World map (web/admin/assets/maps/world-110m.svg): Natural Earth 1:110m admin-0 countries (public
  domain, https://www.naturalearthdata.com) through the world-atlas 2.0.2 npm package, Copyright
  2013-2019 Michael Bostock, ISC (LICENSES/ISC.txt; https://github.com/topojson/world-atlas),
  converted by tools/worldmap/topo2svg.py.
* DB-IP IP to Country Lite: IP geolocation by DB-IP (https://db-ip.com). The "IP to Country Lite"
  database is licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License
  (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/, LICENSES/CC-BY-4.0.txt). The Docker image ships an
  unmodified copy at /usr/share/wpgo/geoip/country.mmdb, and sites download the monthly release
  into their data directory (internal/server/geoip.go). Pursae Analytics shows the attribution on
  its Settings screen.
* Translations (web/languages/wpgo-*.json, 135 locales): translations of Pursae's own interface
  strings, written for Pursae (git history; the files carry no translate.wordpress.org headers),
  GPLv2 or later like the rest of Pursae. WordPress' own language packs are not bundled: a site
  downloads them from translate.wordpress.org when an administrator picks a language (GPLv2 or
  later, WordPress translators).


